-- #1269 MIRROR PROBE (resolve's `Env.ifaceMethods`, `compiler/frontend/resolve.mdk`)
-- -- the severity-ladder half of this fix.
--
-- #1269's own fix turns an exit-1 rejection into an exit-0 acceptance (a correct
-- `impl` that used to collide with an unrelated same-named interface's method set).
-- Per AGENTS.md, "does this fix turn a path that returned NOTHING into one that
-- returns SOMETHING? If so, the new something is UNTESTED BY CONSTRUCTION" -- every
-- pre-existing fixture covered the rejecting case, so none of them can fail if the
-- fix over-widens and starts accepting method names it must not.
--
-- So this fixture is the mirror, in TWO cells:
--   * `impl Solo X` supplies `wrongName`, not `Solo`'s only method `rightName` --
--     genuinely wrong, with NO same-name interface anywhere in the graph.  Must
--     still reject with R-METHOD-NOT-IN-INTERFACE.
--   * `impl Same2 P` supplies `gandThen2` -- a name that means NOTHING in
--     `pmod2.Same2` (its only method is `pmth2`) but IS a real method of
--     `gmod2.Same2`, the unrelated same-named interface that is in this graph but
--     never imported here (only `gdummy2` is imported from `gmod2`).  This is the
--     sharp form of the mirror: the pre-fix code's first-match bug would have
--     resolved `Same2` to `gmod2.Same2` (imported first, in source order) and
--     ACCEPTED `gandThen2` as a valid member -- a false ACCEPT, not merely a false
--     reject, on a method name that has no meaning in the interface actually in
--     scope.  The fix must resolve `Same2` to `pmod2.Same2` (the only one this file
--     imports) and reject `gandThen2` against it.  COUNTERFACTUAL, RUN: reverting
--     `oneImportIfaceMethods`/`filterIfaceMethods` to the pre-fix bare-name filter
--     makes this cell's R-METHOD-NOT-IN-INTERFACE for `gandThen2` DISAPPEAR (while
--     `Solo`'s cell is unaffected, since `Solo` has no collision) -- confirmed on
--     this binary, not asserted.
import gmod2.{gdummy2}
import pmod2.{Same2, pmth2}
import soloiface.{Solo, rightName}

data X = MkX

impl Solo X where
  wrongName x = 1

data P a b = MkP a b

impl Same2 P where
  gandThen2 p = gandThen2 p

n : Int
n = gdummy2 1
